 The method follows a greedy acceptance strategy,
 since a newly generated chromosome replaces the current chromosome only when it achieves a lower classification error.
 Furthermore,
 each accepted chromosome is immediately used in the subsequent crossover operation,
 allowing improvements obtained during successive crossover trials to be accumulated.
\end_layout

