 The corresponding classification task aims to assign each sample to one of the ten digit classes,
 ranging from 0 to 9 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "penbased"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Phoneme
\series default
.
 The Phoneme dataset contains acoustic measurements extracted from speech signals.
 The corresponding classification task aims to distinguish between nasal and oral phonemes based on their acoustic characteristics 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "phoneme"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
PirVision.
 
\series default
The PirVision dataset contains sensor measurements collected for occupancy detection.
 The corresponding classification task aims to determine occupancy status based on data acquired from passive infrared (PIR) sensing devices 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "pirvision"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Satimage
\series default
.
 The Satimage dataset contains multispectral satellite image data representing different types of terrain.
 The corresponding classification task aims to assign image regions to different land-cover classes based on their spectral characteristics 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "satimage"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Segment.
 
\series default
The Segment dataset contains image regions characterized by a set of numerical features extracted from outdoor images.
 The corresponding classification task aims to assign each region to one of several image categories based on its visual characteristics 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "segment"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Shuttle.
 
\series default
The Shuttle dataset was originally developed to derive comprehensible classification rules for determining the conditions under which automatic landing control of a spacecraft would be preferable to manual control.
 The corresponding classification task involves distinguishing among different operational conditions based on a set of numerical measurements.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Spambase
\series default
.
 The Spambase dataset contains features extracted from email messages,
 including word and character frequencies as well as information related to sequences of capital letters.
 The corresponding binary classification task aims to distinguish spam from non-spam emails 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "spambase"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Spiral
\series default
,
 which is an artificial dataset.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Student.
 
\series default
The Student dataset contains educational data collected from 587 students over two consecutive academic years in ten non-university educational centers.
 The attributes describe factors such as academic performance,
 student abilities,
 motivation,
 and methodological and assessment preferences.
 The corresponding classification task aims to categorize students according to their educational characteristics and performance 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "student"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Splice
\series default
 dataset,
 which is inspired by biology.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Texture.

\series default
 The Texture dataset is designed for the classification of different visual textures and comprises 11 texture classes,
 including grass lawn,
 pressed calf leather,
 handmade paper,
 raffia,
 and cotton canvas.
 Each pattern corresponds to a pixel represented by 40 numerical features obtained from the estimation of fourth-order modified moments computed at four different orientations
\begin_inset Formula $:\ensuremath{0^{\circ}},\ensuremath{45^{\circ}},\ensuremath{90^{\circ}},$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $135^{\circ}$
\end_inset

.
 The corresponding classification task aims to assign each pattern to one of the 11 texture categories 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "texture"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Thyroid.
 
\series default
The Thyroid dataset contains clinical measurements related to thyroid gland function.
 The corresponding classification task aims to determine whether a patient exhibits normal thyroid function or suffers from hyperthyroidism or hypothyroidism,
 resulting in a three-class classification problem 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "thyroid"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The 
\series bold
TwoNorm
\series default
 dataset is a synthetic 20-dimensional binary classification problem originally introduced by Breiman.
 The patterns of each class are generated from multivariate normal distributions with unit covariance matrices and symmetric mean vectors.
 Specifically,
 the two class means are 
\begin_inset Formula $(a,a,\ldots,a)$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $(-a,-a,\ldots,-a)$
\end_inset

,
 where 
\begin_inset Formula $a=2/\sqrt{20}$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Vehicle.
 
\series default
The Vehicle dataset is designed to classify vehicle silhouettes into four different categories using a set of numerical features extracted from their shapes.
 The silhouettes were obtained from vehicles viewed from different angles,
 making the classification task dependent on distinguishing characteristic geometric properties despite variations in viewing orientation 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "vehicle"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Yeast.
 
\series default
The Yeast dataset contains information describing proteins from Saccharomyces cerevisiae.
 Each protein is represented by eight numerical features derived from sequence-based measurements.
 The corresponding classification task aims to predict the cellular localization site of each protein among ten possible classes 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "yeast"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
EEG.
 The EEG dataset is a medical dataset containing electroencephalographic recordings obtained from healthy subjects and patients with epilepsy under different physiological and pathological conditions 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "eeg1,eeg2"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
 The original dataset consists of five subsets,
 denoted by Z,
 O,
 N,
 F,
 and S,
 corresponding to different recording conditions and brain states.
 From these subsets,
 four classification problems were constructed for the experimental evaluation:
 Z_F_S,
 ZO_NF_S,
 Z_O_N_F_S,
 and ZONF_S.
\end_layout

